1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:21,000
Now is the moment you've all been waiting for. The results are in, and it's time to meet your top 10!

2
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:31,000
All right, prepare yourselves, folks!

3
00:00:51,000 --> 00:01:01,000
In 10th place, 75th generation trainee, Memori Kishida!

4
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:09,000
I'm Memori Kishida!

5
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:29,000
First of all, I'd like to say thank you from the bottom of my heart. I can't believe I'm standing here after dreaming of being a successor for so long. I would be lying if I said it hasn't been a frustrating journey, but through every tear and hardship, my friends were always by my side!

6
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:31,000
Memori...

7
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:51,000
I'm sorry. I'm not very good at expressing my emotions, so I just bottled them up and never showed them. However, because I had friends who always got even more frustrated, who cried and got angry alongside me, because of them, I've been able to keep trying without giving up!

8
00:01:51,000 --> 00:02:04,000
That's not true at all. You saved me by always smiling for me, and by always being there. You supported me every step of the way. That's why I've made it this far.

9
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:13,000
Even though I'm not a successor to have been chosen in the general elections, this is truly my happiest moment!

10
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:31,000
But I still have the promise I made to my friends! Kanata! The general elections are just the beginning of our journey! Let's both become successors as soon as we can, okay?

11
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:39,000
It's like Memori's looking down on us.

12
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:42,000
This is... kind of embarrassing.

13
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:43,000
Yuka?

14
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:50,000
To be painfully honest, I had given up on being elected the moment the election was announced. But she... kept working.

15
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:58,000
I wouldn't be so sure of that! The general elections give everyone an equal opportunity to shine, no matter who they are!

16
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:00,000
I didn't realize how right she was!

17
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:01,000
Mm-hmm.

18
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:04,000
She gives me hope! Let's do our best!

19
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:07,000
Memori-san is amazing!

20
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:11,000
Then... what about Chiyuri?

21
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:18,000
If I'm chosen in the general elections...

22
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:21,000
You'll quit Zero-Zero?

23
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:27,000
Yes, ma'am. If I remain a part of Zero-Zero, I'll only cause trouble for the others.

24
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:31,000
I don't get it. If that's the case, why didn't you say you would quit sooner?

25
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:32,000
What?

26
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:43,000
You were ninth place. True, it was just the preliminaries, but each of those votes came from fans who adore you. What you're planning on doing would be spitting on those feelings.

27
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:57,000
Those votes didn't come from my strength. It was because of Zodiac. They're all being fooled. The only reason I was chosen is because of my father's power.

28
00:03:57,000 --> 00:04:03,000
If you're elected, you'll have to make a speech on stage.

29
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:04,000
Oh!

30
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:15,000
We leave it up to members to decide what they want to say. It's not my place to tell you what to do. But if you intend to quit, tell them yourself when you're up on that stage.

31
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:24,000
If I'm elected, I have to tell them. I have to do it here.

32
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:27,000
Moving on, the ninth place announcement.

33
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:37,000
Your choice for ninth place is...

34
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:40,000
Tenth generation, Sei Miyazawa!

35
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:41,000
Oh, wow!

36
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:43,000
Sei!

37
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:45,000
Sei!

38
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:49,000
I'm so honored! Everyone, thank you for your support!

39
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:51,000
Sei Miyazawa!

40
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:52,000
All right!

41
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:57,000
Hey, Megumi, sit down.

42
00:04:57,000 --> 00:04:58,000
Huh?

43
00:04:58,000 --> 00:04:59,000
Oh, oops.

44
00:04:59,000 --> 00:05:06,000
Megumi-san seems happy.

45
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:07,000
Mm-hmm.

46
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:11,000
I voted for Sonata ten times when the ballots were open.

47
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:12,000
You what?!

48
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:15,000
You should've voted for yourself like I did, Suzu!

49
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:19,000
We shouldn't vote at all! The whole point of this thing is to let the fans choose!

50
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:21,000
And voting for yourself?!

51
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:23,000
Leave it to Sonata to get Yuka riled!

52
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:24,000
Ugh!

53
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:35,000
Come on, now!

54
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:40,000
Ah! Yuka could appear during the broadcast at any moment, you piece of junk!

55
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:44,000
Ugh! I bet this is the D.E.S. is doing!

56
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:47,000
That's right. It couldn't possibly be that you never take care of that thing!

57
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:49,000
Oh!

58
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:51,000
Come on, Dad! You can fix anything!

59
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:52,000
Hurry up! Hurry up!

60
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:53,000
Hurry up!

61
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:55,000
Oh, sure! Just leave it to me!

62
00:05:56,000 --> 00:06:01,000
I'm sorry about this, Motomiya-san. You came all the way here to see the broadcast.

63
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:05,000
It's all right. I just hope that I'm not bothering you by coming here and loitering.

64
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:11,000
My husband will be at work for a while longer, and I felt so nervous watching it at home by myself.

65
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:18,000
I understand. Well, we're probably not missing much. They're so new, it might be tough for them to be elected.

66
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:24,000
I know. It's just... my daughter's not very good with competitions.

67
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:40,000
Everyone seems so unhappy. I don't like this. It's scary.

68
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:46,000
In 8th place is... 11th generation, Tomomi Itano!

69
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:51,000
Tomo-chi-pa's already being announced!

70
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:54,000
But she was third in the preliminary announcement!

71
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:55,000
That's not the chance!

72
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:56,000
She was third again!

73
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:58,000
Tomo-chi-pa's already being announced!

74
00:06:58,000 --> 00:07:00,000
Tomo-chi-pa's already being announced!

75
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:03,000
I'm Tomo-mi. Thank you very much.

76
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:06,000
Tomo-chi-pa's already being announced!

77
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:10,000
This is my first time to be participating in the general elections.

78
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:16,000
My older sister, the 10th Tomo-mi, stood in this very spot in the last election.

79
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:23,000
It's tradition that all daughters of the Itano household must audition for AKB-0048.

80
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:31,000
In order to learn, I sat in the audience just like you and watched.

81
00:07:31,440 --> 00:07:34,000
My sister was 8th place.

82
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:39,000
Just like me, she had fallen a considerable number of ranks from the initial results.

83
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:44,000
My sister overcame her tears and smiled during her speech.

84
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:50,000
But as I look around me, I could see her fans sobbing and heartbroken.

85
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:53,000
It was as though they were crying in her place.

86
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:57,000
For the first time in my life, I felt jealous of my sister.

87
00:07:57,000 --> 00:08:02,000
I wished to join Zero Zero and be loved by everyone just like her.

88
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:05,000
Not just for my family, but for myself.

89
00:08:05,000 --> 00:08:10,000
Looking out at the audience, I can see people crying for me,

90
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:13,000
just like they did for my sister that day.

91
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:21,000
Next time, I'd like to see you cry tears of joy instead of tears of frustration.

92
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:28,000
I'll work harder than ever before and be worthy of tears.

93
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:32,000
I am honored to achieve the same rake as my sister.

94
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:35,000
Thank you for staying with me this far.

95
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:42,000
I never thought I'd see her cry like that.

96
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:44,000
I know, right?

97
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:48,000
I'm a really big fan and I've decided to support you.

98
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:49,000
I'll make sure you're elected.

99
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:52,000
I'll do my best for the general elections, too.

100
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:54,000
I never realized.

101
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:58,000
Our fans put their hopes and love into us.

102
00:08:58,000 --> 00:08:59,000
I'm jealous.

103
00:08:59,000 --> 00:09:00,000
I'm jealous.

104
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:01,000
Huh?

105
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:07,000
If you get to stand on that stage, you have an opportunity to answer the fans' love and return it to them.

106
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:08,000
Yeah.

107
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:10,000
Someday I want to thank them.

108
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:13,000
And I'll do it from up on that stage.

109
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:14,000
They're right.

110
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:16,000
We're not alone.

111
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:22,000
We can work with the people who love us and return that love in kind.

112
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:24,000
That's what the general elections are about.

113
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:25,000
Yeah.

114
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:35,000
In seventh place, eighth generation, Haruna Kojima.

115
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:38,000
Thank you very much for voting for me.

116
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:41,000
You're the reason I'm standing here tonight.

117
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:44,000
It's been a while since my last general elections.

118
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:47,000
So I was hoping we could have fun together.

119
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:50,000
And we have.

120
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:54,000
I was shocked to find out I was fifth place in the preliminary results.

121
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:59,000
But really, but receiving seventh place today feels just right.

122
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:02,000
And I can't thank you enough for everything.

123
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:14,000
I'm so frustrated!

124
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:17,000
Koji Haru-san!

125
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:22,000
A place where the always cheerful Koji Haru-san can cry her heart out.

126
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:25,000
A place where she can admit she's frustrated.

127
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:28,000
The general elections are amazing!

128
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:33,000
Because of my father's power, I gained more fans.

129
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:36,000
But I couldn't accept it.

130
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:39,000
Those votes didn't come from my strength.

131
00:10:39,000 --> 00:10:41,000
It was because of Zodiac.

132
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:42,000
And I'm so sorry.

133
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:43,000
I'm so sorry.

134
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:44,000
I'm sorry.

135
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:45,000
I'm sorry.

136
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:46,000
I'm sorry.

137
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:47,000
I'm sorry.

138
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:48,000
I'm sorry.

139
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:49,000
I'm sorry.

140
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:50,000
I'm sorry.

141
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:51,000
I'm sorry.

142
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:52,000
I'm sorry.

143
00:10:52,000 --> 00:10:53,000
I'm sorry.

144
00:10:53,000 --> 00:10:54,000
I'm sorry.

145
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:55,000
I'm sorry.

146
00:10:55,000 --> 00:10:56,000
I'm sorry.

147
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:58,000
It was because of Zodiac.

148
00:10:58,000 --> 00:11:00,000
They're all being fooled!

149
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:02,000
Not my strength.

150
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:04,000
Just my father's power.

151
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:06,000
What am I saying?

152
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:15,000
All the people who voted for me,

153
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:17,000
no matter how they reached that decision,

154
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:21,000
they all like me.

155
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:25,000
They're all people who love me.

156
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:26,000
Moving on.

157
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:28,000
The sixth place announcement.

158
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:29,000
Uh...

159
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:30,000
Chiyari?

160
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:31,000
What's wrong?

161
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:32,000
I'm in...

162
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:33,000
In such an amazing place.

163
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:34,000
In such a wonderful place.

164
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:35,000
I can't do it.

165
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:36,000
I don't want to graduate.

166
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:37,000
What are you talking about?

167
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:39,000
What are you talking about?

168
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:40,000
Graduate?

169
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:57,000
In sixth place is 77th generation trainee, Chiyari Zodo!

170
00:11:57,000 --> 00:11:58,000
Yes.

171
00:11:58,000 --> 00:12:02,000
What are you looking up there?

172
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:16,180
Chiarijan, are you all right?

173
00:12:20,140 --> 00:12:21,500
Chiarijan's acting weird.

174
00:12:21,660 --> 00:12:23,120
Don't worry, it's pretty calming.

175
00:12:23,460 --> 00:12:24,480
It can be overwhelming.

176
00:12:24,920 --> 00:12:26,740
Many members have hyperventilated before.

177
00:12:27,460 --> 00:12:28,260
She'll be fine.

178
00:12:28,880 --> 00:12:30,160
I hope you're right.

179
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:35,060
Chiarijan's the last person I expected to lose it so badly.

180
00:12:49,500 --> 00:12:52,700
Chiarijan, are you able to stand by on your own?

181
00:12:54,280 --> 00:12:56,000
Okay, give it your best.

182
00:12:57,200 --> 00:13:01,280
I have this 77th generation.

183
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:11,380
Trainee, Chiarijan's the last person I have to say it.

184
00:13:12,020 --> 00:13:13,520
I have to tell them.

185
00:13:14,280 --> 00:13:17,060
All right, Chiarijan, it's time to show us your decision.

186
00:13:17,060 --> 00:13:17,520
Chiarijan, what?

187
00:13:17,520 --> 00:13:17,540
What?

188
00:13:18,440 --> 00:13:23,440
I... I... I am... I'm going to...

189
00:13:23,440 --> 00:13:33,440
I... I just want to say...

190
00:13:33,440 --> 00:13:38,720
I... I... I love each and every one of you!

191
00:13:38,720 --> 00:13:44,100
Chiarijan...

192
00:13:44,100 --> 00:13:45,100
Chiarijan...

193
00:13:45,100 --> 00:13:47,340
I love you.

194
00:13:48,020 --> 00:13:49,540
I wouldn't be here without you.

195
00:13:49,720 --> 00:13:52,440
Without my friends and my fans, I'd still be lost.

196
00:13:52,440 --> 00:13:58,920
I want to continue to be a member of AKB-0048 with all of the people that I love.

197
00:14:01,820 --> 00:14:02,820
We love you too!

198
00:14:02,820 --> 00:14:09,040
I can't believe she said that!

199
00:14:09,400 --> 00:14:10,080
Amazing!

200
00:14:10,380 --> 00:14:11,880
I could never be that direct.

201
00:14:12,200 --> 00:14:14,580
This is nothing like the AKB trials were.

202
00:14:14,920 --> 00:14:15,920
What's wrong with her?

203
00:14:16,100 --> 00:14:17,180
She's acting all weird.

204
00:14:17,540 --> 00:14:17,880
Maybe.

205
00:14:18,400 --> 00:14:20,240
But I really understand how she feels.

206
00:14:20,260 --> 00:14:21,460
I'll continue to work hard.

207
00:14:21,820 --> 00:14:23,160
Thank you very much!

208
00:14:27,160 --> 00:14:28,000
Chiarijan...

209
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:30,520
Chiarijan's so brilliant.

210
00:14:31,820 --> 00:14:33,360
And so far away.

211
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:38,280
I guess Chiarijan can be cute when the conditions are right.

212
00:14:38,800 --> 00:14:40,440
I hope she's sure of herself.

213
00:14:41,200 --> 00:14:44,540
In fifth place is Mark III, Mayu Watanabe!

214
00:14:45,320 --> 00:14:46,760
Thank you for your support.

215
00:14:47,020 --> 00:14:48,760
I look forward to many years with you all.

216
00:14:54,600 --> 00:14:57,080
In fourth place, sixth generation,

217
00:14:57,080 --> 00:14:58,720
Yuki Kashiwagi!

218
00:15:00,820 --> 00:15:03,920
I'm aiming for the top and I won't stop till I'm there.

219
00:15:04,380 --> 00:15:06,260
I'll make you fall in love with me.

220
00:15:10,780 --> 00:15:12,140
I don't know about you,

221
00:15:12,220 --> 00:15:13,620
but I'm pretty sure there's no chance

222
00:15:13,620 --> 00:15:15,680
our names aren't getting called this time around.

223
00:15:16,520 --> 00:15:18,640
Maybe, but I still think it's amazing

224
00:15:18,640 --> 00:15:20,260
that two trainees were selected.

225
00:15:20,360 --> 00:15:22,160
Yeah, it really is amazing,

226
00:15:22,340 --> 00:15:23,980
but I don't know.

227
00:15:23,980 --> 00:15:32,700
Something's not right.

228
00:15:33,440 --> 00:15:34,840
My legs feel cold.

229
00:15:35,760 --> 00:15:37,760
Maybe the air conditioning's too strong.

230
00:15:37,760 --> 00:15:43,420
In third place is 10th generation,

231
00:15:43,860 --> 00:15:45,000
Sayaka Akimono!

232
00:15:45,620 --> 00:15:47,720
Thank you so much, everyone!

233
00:15:51,500 --> 00:15:52,980
Thank you, thank you!

234
00:15:53,100 --> 00:15:54,320
I can't say it enough!

235
00:15:54,420 --> 00:15:55,100
What is this?

236
00:15:55,620 --> 00:15:56,760
I can't hear anyone.

237
00:15:56,760 --> 00:16:05,640
I can't see Chiari very well, either.

238
00:16:09,140 --> 00:16:10,020
Now then,

239
00:16:10,240 --> 00:16:12,040
there are only two seats remaining.

240
00:16:12,400 --> 00:16:14,300
Who will our top two members be?

241
00:16:17,600 --> 00:16:18,600
Here we go.

242
00:16:18,600 --> 00:16:20,700
Hold on to your seats, folks.

243
00:16:20,700 --> 00:16:29,800
With 1,184,848 points,

244
00:16:30,160 --> 00:16:32,480
your second place winner is...

245
00:16:32,480 --> 00:16:35,160
5th generation Minami Takahashi!

246
00:16:35,160 --> 00:16:50,120
Step right up, Takemina!

247
00:16:54,760 --> 00:16:57,900
I'm 5th generation Minami Takahashi.

248
00:16:57,900 --> 00:17:03,000
Thank you all for your support.

249
00:17:03,640 --> 00:17:05,820
The general elections answered a question,

250
00:17:06,320 --> 00:17:08,440
one I've had in my heart for a while now.

251
00:17:09,420 --> 00:17:11,480
Those who succeed Minami Takahashi

252
00:17:11,480 --> 00:17:13,520
have been captains of Zero Zero,

253
00:17:13,900 --> 00:17:15,900
and I've done my very best

254
00:17:15,900 --> 00:17:18,260
to support my members as their captain.

255
00:17:18,680 --> 00:17:20,460
But I may have been wrong.

